skills.card:
factorial — Work out a factorial — multiply every whole number from 1 up to n together.
  needs: n: integer
  e.g. "what is 10 factorial" → {"n":10}

fractionSimplify — Reduce a fraction like 6/8 to its lowest terms.
  needs: fraction: string
  e.g. "simplify 6/8" → {"fraction":"6/8"}

gcd — Find the biggest number that divides them all exactly.
  needs: values: array
  e.g. "greatest common divisor of 48 and 18" → {"values":[48,18]}

isPrime — Say whether a whole number is prime, and give a divisor if it is not.
  needs: value: integer
  e.g. "is 97 prime" → {"value":97}

lcm — Find the smallest number they all go into.
  needs: values: array
  e.g. "lowest common multiple of 4 and 6" → {"values":[4,6]}

parseNumber — Read a number written any human way — "1.2k", "$3,400", "three quarters of a million" — as a plain number.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "what number is 1.2k" → {"text":"1.2k"}

percentChange — Percentage change between two numbers, and the difference in plain terms.
  needs: from: number, to: number
  e.g. "my rent went from 1200 to 1350, what percent increase is that" → {"from":1200,"to":1350}

percentOf — Take a percentage of a number — 15% of 240, or 20 percent of a bill.
  needs: percent: number, value: number
  e.g. "what is 15% of 240" → {"percent":15,"value":240}

primeFactors — Break a whole number down into the prime numbers it is made of.
  needs: value: integer
  e.g. "prime factors of 360" → {"value":360}

product — Multiply a list of numbers you give together.
  needs: values: array
  e.g. "multiply 12 by 8 by 3" → {"values":[12,8,3]}

ratioSolve — Solve a proportion when one of the four terms is missing.
  optional: a: number, b: number, c: number, d: number
  e.g. "solve this proportion, 3 is to 4 as 9 is to what" → {"a":3,"b":4,"c":9}

solveQuadratic — Solve a quadratic equation — the roots of ax² + bx + c = 0, real or complex.
  needs: a: number, b: number, c: number
  e.g. "solve x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0" → {"a":1,"b":-5,"c":6}

sum — Add a list of numbers up to one final total.
  needs: values: array
  e.g. "add up 1250, 3400 and 890" → {"values":[1250,3400,890]}

whatPercent — Work out what share one number is of another, as a percentage — what proportion 18 is of 24, or a score out of a maximum.
  needs: part: number, whole: number
  e.g. "36 out of 240 as a percentage" → {"part":36,"whole":240}

haversineDistance — Work out the great-circle distance between two points on Earth from their latitude and longitude.
  needs: lat1: number, lon1: number, lat2: number, lon2: number
  e.g. "distance from london to paris" → {"lat1":51.5074,"lon1":-0.1278,"lat2":48.8566,"lon2":2.3522}

pythagorean — Find a missing side of a right-angled triangle — a ladder's length, a diagonal, a hypotenuse — from the other two.
  optional: a: number, b: number, c: number
  e.g. "hypotenuse of a triangle with sides 3 and 4" → {"a":3,"b":4}

